Review written to `docs/reviews/physics-constants/phys-const-15-stefan-boltzmann-precision.md`.

**Summary**: The HARES constant `5.670_374_419e-8` is correct and f64 preserves full CODATA 2018 precision — the 53-bit mantissa provides ~5 extra guard digits beyond the 10 significant digits needed. ULP is ~6.62×10⁻²⁴, far smaller than the last digit's place value of 1×10⁻¹⁸.

All three findings are confirmation/nit, not defects:
- **Medium**: HARES is the most precise of the three codebases (EnergyPlus uses outdated 5.6697e-8; OCHRE has two inconsistent inline values with no named constant)
- **Low**: The test at line 282 is tautological (same literal in both sides)
- **Low**: f64 is adequate — no type change needed
